-- Nested spans on one thread; finish in reverse start order.
public define span as opaque.
public use "trace" function begin(name text) giving failable pointer to span.
public use "trace" function current giving unsigned.
public use "trace" function identity(value pointer to span) giving failable unsigned.
public use "trace" function parent(value pointer to span) giving failable unsigned.
-- Returns independently owned text.
public use "trace" function name(value pointer to span) giving failable text.
-- Finishes the active span and returns its monotonic duration in nanoseconds.
public use "trace" function finish(value pointer to span) giving failable unsigned.
public use "trace" function elapsed(value pointer to span) giving failable unsigned.
-- A span must be finished before close; both operations use its creating thread.
public use "trace" function close(value pointer to span) giving failable nothing.
